# UST.G3BP H11 Endpoint Determinant CRT Screen Theorem v1

## Result

Let `C_0(gamma)` be the selected `5439 x 5439` H11 chart used by the split-prime source pipeline and let `C_*(gamma)` be the same chart after the exact G3BI endpoint correction is inserted. For each of the eight certified completely split primes

```text
21817, 33863, 37493, 38113, 68213, 69011, 72271, 73673,
```

the selected sextic has six distinct roots. G3BP constructs `C_*(gamma)` at every one of these 48 roots and computes its determinant by exact finite-field sparse elimination.

All 48 determinants are nonzero. Thus the selected endpoint H11 chart is invertible at all 48 tested split places. This strengthens the one-place existence certificate of G3BN without claiming that finitely many residue checks alone prove a universal characteristic-zero statement.

## CRT screen

At each prime, the six determinant values interpolate uniquely to the six power-basis coordinates of one element of the selected degree-six number-field residue algebra. The first seven primes were used as a reconstruction prefix and the eighth was withheld.

The centered seven-prime candidates predict `0/6` withheld coordinates. The centered eight-prime candidate also evaluates to `3` at `(p,gamma)=(11,3)`, while the independently computed endpoint determinant there is `0`.

Therefore the existing modulus does **not** identify the integral determinant coordinates. In particular, the centered CRT representative cannot be promoted to the characteristic-zero determinant.

## What is closed

G3BP closes the following finite statement:

1. the exact G3BI endpoint chart was constructed at 48 certified split roots;
2. every one of those charts is invertible;
3. all eight six-coordinate determinant residues were emitted exactly;
4. the existing eight-prime centered reconstruction fails both an independent holdout and the GF(11) screen.

## What remains open

This theorem does not reconstruct the determinant in `Z[gamma]`, prove a determinant height bound, reconstruct the H11 action over `Q(gamma)`, or produce the terminal physical readout. Exact promotion requires additional split primes in this six-scalar channel until independent holdouts stabilize, together with a proved coefficient-height bound. Only then may the modular G3BO action be denominator-cleared and reconstructed through its adjugate-action tensor.

